From ef958666571ec46c8c1c44b8de0e799acce52f89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mario Behn <mario.behn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:39:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] cpdetect: blind cyclic-prefix (CP-OFDM) detector, host
 tool and board app

The PSD classifier sees power only. The cyclic prefix is a phase-coherent
repetition in the complex samples, so this finds FFT size, guard length,
symbol timing and fractional carrier offset of an OFDM signal from
time-domain IQ without knowing the standard.

- tools/cpdetect/cpdetect.py: numpy reference with a CLI and a selftest
- tools/cpdetect/link_test.py: cabled two-board check
- app/cpdetect: the same algorithm and thresholds in C (libiio or file),
  JSON output and optional MQTT publish under state/cpdetect
- package/cpdetect: Buildroot package, not enabled in any defconfig

Checked on hardware (Pluto TX to Pluto+ RX through a 40 dB attenuator):
OFDM N=1024/256/2048 found with the right guard, CW tone, single-carrier
QPSK and noise rejected, the C binary matches the Python results and runs
on the Pluto+ ARM in about 0.25 s per analysis. The package was
cross-compiled by hand, not built through a full Buildroot run.

Signed-off-by: Mario Behn <mario.behn@gmail.com>
